From 097e35cac4b7231383a012f9c8bf275cce9b64f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 19:06:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] target/dadao: add decodetree instruction decode skeleton
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the QEMU decodetree-based instruction decoder for DADAO SimRISC M1:

- insn.decode: defines all 87 M1 instructions with field/format/pattern
  declarations matching spec.md §2.3 and §2.8 opcode map
- translate.c: replaces manual decode_opc with decode() call, adds
  trans_ stubs for all instructions (swym as NOP, rest as ILLI)
- meson.build: integrates decodetree generation via decodetree.process()

MISC-Norm (op=0x10) uses a grouped sub-decode block by ha[5:0].
All other opcodes decode by the full 8-bit op value.
Reserved encodings fall through to UNDI exception.
---
 target/dadao/insn.decode | 190 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 target/dadao/meson.build |   4 +
 target/dadao/translate.c | 115 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 308 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 target/dadao/insn.decode

